# The sandbox with no window: what this build wired, and whether the projects load.
#
#     cd apps/sandbox-heaps
#     haxe check.hxml
#
# Seconds rather than minutes, because it is the same host without heaps or a window under it, so it
# answers "is the setup right" separately from "does the app build", which are the two questions that
# otherwise get debugged as one.
#
# In a checkout of this repository, point the haxelib at it first, so `-lib hxscript` resolves and
# `extraParams.hxml` applies. That file is the whole of the setup:
#
#     haxelib dev hxscript ../..
#
# **Heaps cannot be added to this one.** The sandbox for lime can be asked `-lib flixel` and will
# report what a script could then reach, but heaps does not compile under eval: `hxd.fmt.hmd` fails
# to type and `hlsdl` reaches the `hl` package, which eval refuses. So a project extending an h2d
# class is reported here as extending a base this build does not carry, which is true and is as far
# as a windowless check can get. What it still answers is everything else: the setup, the projects
# on disk, whether each parses, and what each would run.
#
# `--run` rather than `-main ... --interp`, because only `--run` passes arguments through. Check's own
# arguments do go after, for the same reason:
#
#     haxe check.hxml --projects ../some/other/folder

-lib hxscript
-cp .

# Names the sandbox's own classes to hxScript, so `@:scriptable` on them means something.
-D hxscript_host=host

--run Check
